In addition to running commands in a pod, you can also port-forward
network connections from a Pod to code running on the local machine. Like
exec, the port forwarded traffic goes over a WebSocket. It is up to your
code what it does with this port forwarded socket. You could simply send a
single request and receive a response as a string of bytes, or you could build
a complete proxy server (like what kubectl port-forward does) to
serve arbitrary requests through this proxy.

